WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.258 --> 00:00:03.550
Please welcome Marlee Matlin, Troy Kotsur,

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.753
and their interpreters, Jack and Justin.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.247
(audience applauding)

4
00:00:23.546 --> 00:00:24.379
Thank you.

5
00:00:26.588 --> 00:00:29.484
(Drew squeals)

6
00:00:29.484 --> 00:00:32.440
Oh, Jack, I'm so happy to see you.

7
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.527
Hello, nice to meet you.

8
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.090
Jack and I have known each other for-

9
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.363
And Marlee.
And Marlee, obviously.

10
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.283
Actually, Marlee, how long have we known each other?

11
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.880
Well, we've known each other really a long time.

12
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.020
A long time probably than we actually realize.

13
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.010
Do you remember how we met?

14
00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:56.893
Do you remember when we met?

15
00:00:56.893 --> 00:00:58.810
Yes, yes.
You do?

16
00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.480
Actually, let me tell you, let me tell the story.

17
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.380
Yes, okay, go.

18
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.213
Ready, ready?

19
00:01:03.213 --> 00:01:04.410
Okay, here we go.

20
00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:08.470 line:15%
So we were in the, it was a bar,

21
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.960 line:15%
it was called the Columbus Bar and Grill,

22
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.140 line:15%
and it was the night of this crazy award ceremony

23
00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.270
that we went to with my old boyfriend who won that night.

24
00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:20.960
And William Hurt, Michael Douglas, Raúl Juliá.

25
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.140
Yes, I knew it!
Yes.

26
00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.140
And so we got into the bar, it was like one in the morning,

27
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.383
and I was a little bit sort of buzzed, but anyway,

28
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.873
more than necessary really,

29
00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:36.860
and we walked in and we sat down,

30
00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.580
and someone comes up and says, "Hi, welcome.

31
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.050
What would you like to drink?"

32
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:46.990
And I looked, I was like, "What?

33
00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:47.823
ET?"

34
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.020
No, I was so thrown.

35
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.960
It was you, all of you, this big, this big.

36
00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.810
And William hurt flipped out when he saw you

37
00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.340
because you guys did a movie together.

38
00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.857
Oh my gosh, so he played-
So mad.

39
00:02:01.857 --> 00:02:05.461
He was mad.
That's right.

40
00:02:05.461 --> 00:02:06.961
Did he hold me up?

41
00:02:08.223 --> 00:02:09.326
Yeah, I think he did.

42
00:02:09.326 --> 00:02:10.720
Yes.

43
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:11.810
You were this much.

44
00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.370
Yeah.

45
00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:17.340
Because I played his daughter in "Altered States."

46
00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.420
I know.

47
00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.330
And yes, he treated me like his daughter, that's right.

48
00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.270
I remember that, yeah.

49
00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.040
He was mad at me and he held me up.

50
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.130
Yeah.

51
00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.640
It was a very interesting journey since then.

52
00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.030
It's been an interesting journey since then.

53
00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:32.950
But since that moment, I remember many times

54
00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:37.143
and many years feeling very comfortable and safe with you.

55
00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:39.723
Me too.

56
00:02:39.723 --> 00:02:42.120
The world wasn't always so comfortable and safe.

57
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.100
I know, I know.

58
00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.430
But when I was with you.

59
00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.263
Yeah.

60
00:02:46.658 --> 00:02:48.780
I appreciate that you said that.

61
00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.122
And I was so excited to see you.

62
00:02:52.122 --> 00:02:52.955
Thank you.

63
00:02:52.955 --> 00:02:57.810
And I love this film so much.

64
00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:03.770
And Troy, first of all, your performance is so beautiful.

65
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.230
And I loved that you had watched Marlee

66
00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:12.793
win the Oscar for Best Actress.

67
00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.553
Is that in 1987?

68
00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.770
5 years ago.

69
00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.240
Yeah, exactly.

70
00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.900
Around that time, I was a senior in high school.

71
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.823
So you can do the math and figure out what my age was.

72
00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.260
35 years ago, 35 years ago.

73
00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:30.640
What she said.

74
00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.270
It was the first time I saw authentic deaf representation

75
00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.370
on screen in "Children of a Lesser God."

76
00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.430
It really inspired me and I felt connected.

77
00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:43.890 line:15%
And it really gave me hope as an actor to pursue acting.

78
00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.000 line:15%
And so I continued for many years as an actor

79
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.110
and it led me to get to this point.

80
00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:53.340
And it's been truly amazing to finally work with Marlee.

81
00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.940
She's just a foot away from me right now.

82
00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.635
And I never thought that would happen.

83
00:03:57.635 --> 00:04:00.802
(audience applauding)

84
00:04:01.851 --> 00:04:05.430
And you have that chemistry.

85
00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.960
And Troy, you're making history now yourself

86
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.273
as being the first deaf actor to be nominated.

87
00:04:13.952 --> 00:04:16.280
(audience applauding)

88
00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.010
Thank you, love you all.

89
00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:22.970
When you see this film, this is a no-brainer,

90
00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.780
but how is the full circle moment being next to Marlee,

91
00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.663
who inspired you back then?

92
00:04:33.728 --> 00:04:36.150
Well, it was such an interesting timeline for me.

93
00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.770
So Marlee was very young, won the award,

94
00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.290
and I was inspired, and I remained true to my vision.

95
00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.880
I was patient with all of the frustration and politics

96
00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.100
and oppression and all that.

97
00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.910
And finally reached this point, looking at her,

98
00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.320
I finally feel like we understand each other.

99
00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.850
We are able to share this journey

100
00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.740
and this experience together and help each other out

101
00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.380
and help Hollywood to begin to improve opening their minds,

102
00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.060
to begin thinking outside the box

103
00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:02.420
and all those types of things,

104
00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:05.960
because the deaf community has so many stories to tell.

105
00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.910
You know, for Troy, I think knowing,

106
00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.500
after 35 years since I won the Oscar,

107
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.450
and I've seen so much and I've plowed through all the-

108
00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.700
I mean, it's been an interesting journey.

109
00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.460
Really, a wonderful one, but at the same time,

110
00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.610
compared to what might have happened in the past up to now,

111
00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:26.830
I think now more eyes are open, more ears are open,

112
00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:31.210
more people are aware of our community, of our culture,

113
00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.090
our beautiful language, American Sign Language,

114
00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:37.310
and there's a lot more opportunities.

115
00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.550
And yet, there's still more work to do.

116
00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.870
But one thing I've been seeing is

117
00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.020
there is more collaboration.

118
00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:48.460
There are deaf actors, directors, writers,

119
00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:51.000
who are working with those of us in the business

120
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.930
who happen to be working with us.

121
00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:53.880
So we're collaborating.

122
00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.436
And I think collaboration is the key these days.

123
00:05:56.436 --> 00:05:59.019
(upbeat music)

